---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro"
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Judgment Pairs — Culture Explorer"
  description="Beauty argued by comparison: what endured beside what we accept. Domes, towers, and civilizational standards."
>
  <div class="page-hero with-photo">
    <img
      src="https://images.pexels.com/photos/753639/pexels-photo-753639.jpeg?auto=compress&cs=tinysrgb&w=2000"
      alt=""
    />
    <div class="wrap-narrow">
      <div class="kicker">Beauty is argued by comparison</div>
      <h1>What endured. What we accept.</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Do not debate taste in the abstract. Place two facades beside each other and let the eye finish the sentence.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <section style="padding-top:0">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="compare">
        <figure>
          <img
            src="https://images.pexels.com/photos/753639/pexels-photo-753639.jpeg?auto=compress&cs=tinysrgb&w=1800"
            alt="St. Peter's Basilica at dusk"
          />
          <figcaption>
            <strong>A dome that still organizes a city.</strong> Built to lift the eye, last, and be loved by people not yet born.
          </figcaption>
        </figure>
        <figure>
          <img
            src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1486325212027-8081e485255e?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1600&q=80"
            alt="Curtain-wall glass tower"
          />
          <figcaption>
            <strong>A tower that could belong to any country.</strong> Built to be leased, photographed, and replaced.
          </figcaption>
        </figure>
      </div>

      <div class="wrap-narrow" style="margin-top:3rem">
        <h2>The question is not “which is newer.”</h2>
        <p>
          One building asks for pilgrimage. The other asks for a logo on the fortieth floor. Both are expensive. Only one becomes a memory you would teach a child to honor.
        </p>
        <p>
          Cities like London and Dubai fill with identical glass because we were taught that beauty is subjective, optional, even embarrassing. The past is not embarrassed. It left us the dome.
        </p>
        <p>Now walk your own skyline. Which buildings would you still photograph if the brand names were gone?</p>
        <p>
          <a class="btn" href="/street">Take this eye home</a>
          <a class="btn" href="/see" style="margin-left:0.5rem;">Back to How to See</a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .page-hero.with-photo {
    position: relative;
    min-height: 54vh;
    display: grid;
    place-items: end;
    color: #fff;
    padding: 0 0 4rem;
  }
  .page-hero.with-photo img {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    object-fit: cover;
  }
  .page-hero.with-photo::after {
    content: "";
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    background: linear-gradient(180deg, rgba(12, 9, 6, 0.15), rgba(12, 9, 6, 0.72));
  }
  .page-hero.with-photo .wrap-narrow {
    position: relative;
    z-index: 2;
  }
  .page-hero.with-photo h1 {
    color: #fff;
  }
  .page-hero.with-photo .lede {
    color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.88);
  }
  .page-hero.with-photo .kicker {
    color: #e6c48a;
  }
  .compare {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 14px;
  }
  .compare figure {
    margin: 0;
  }
  .compare img {
    width: 100%;
    height: 58vh;
    object-fit: cover;
  }
  .compare figcaption {
    margin-top: 0.7rem;
    color: var(--ink-2, #3b3228);
  }
  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .compare {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
    .compare img {
      height: 36vh;
    }
  }
</style>